  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level (mean of outcomes), calculating differences between outcomes and this level, and then preferring the lottery with the higher probability of positive differences. In this case, both Lottery A and B have outcomes above the aspiration level (-1668.33), so both have positive differences. However, Lottery A has a 100% chance of a positive difference (-5 > -1668.33), while Lottery B has a 99.9% chance (0 > -1668.33). Thus, Lottery A has a higher probability of positive differences and should be preferred by the reason. However, the individual chose Lottery B, citing the high probability of losing nothing. The individual did not mention the aspiration level, nor did they refer to differences from a mean or to the probability of positive differences. Their justification is based on the emotional appeal of avoiding loss, not on a formal application of the aspiration-level rule. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reasoning in the report is qualitatively different and does not reflect the structure of the decision reason. There is no evidence of computing or referencing the aspiration level or comparing probabilities of positive differences. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
